t because neural networks literally live in curved spacetime, but because many of the spaces that matter in machine learning are themselves curved.1. Why Euclidean space is often the wrong stageStandard deep learning treats parameters and embeddings as points in flat Euclidean space. That assumption is convenient but frequently unrealistic:
Probability distributions form a curved statistical manifold.
