The Fisher–Rao metric turns the space of probability distributions (or the parameter space of a model) into a Riemannian manifold. The natural gradient is the steepest-descent direction with respect to this metric. It is invariant under reparameterization and often converges far more efficiently than ordinary SGD or Adam, especially on highly curved or poorly conditioned loss landscapes.Hyperbolic Embeddings
