Many constraints that appear in deep learning (orthogonality, fixed rank, positive-definiteness) define smooth Riemannian manifolds (Stiefel, Grassmann, SPD manifolds). Riemannian optimization methods (retraction, vector transport, Riemannian Adam, etc.) keep the iterates on the manifold by construction and often yield more stable and interpretable solutions.Geometric Deep Learning more broadly
Networks whose architecture respects the geometry of the domain (graphs, meshes, manifolds) rather than forcing everything into a Euclidean grid.3. Recent developments (2024–2026)Research has moved quickly:
